  "scientific_conclusion": "Empirical evaluation on genuine CSE-CIC-IDS2018 future-day flows confirms that the supervised Random Forest suffers catastrophic recall collapse on unseen attack families (Botnet detection=0.02%, Infiltration detection=0.00%). The unsupervised Isolation Forest trained on early benign traffic substantially improves detection of unseen behavioral attacks, but concept drift in benign traffic causes higher false positive rates across temporal boundaries. Anomaly detection must function as a triage/alerting layer rather than an unconstrained autonomous blocker."
